From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 16:47:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: drv: Stop the pipeline walk at USB Type-C
 connectors

The display engine driver adds every node it finds along the display
pipeline graph as a component, except connectors. A DisplayPort
transmitter in USB Type-C alternate mode ends its graph at the SBU port
of a usb-c-connector node, which no component driver binds, so the
display engine would wait for it forever.

Treat usb-c-connector nodes as connectors, as hdmi-connector nodes are.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: booted on one board; the display engine bound
with the USB Type-C connector at the end of the output path.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_drv.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_drv.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_drv.c
index 5e80d48aad75..c60861cf05ad 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun4i_drv.c
@@ -155,7 +155,8 @@ static const struct component_master_ops sun4i_drv_master_ops = {
 
 static bool sun4i_drv_node_is_connector(struct device_node *node)
 {
-	return of_device_is_compatible(node, "hdmi-connector");
+	return of_device_is_compatible(node, "hdmi-connector") ||
+		of_device_is_compatible(node, "usb-c-connector");
 }
 
 static bool sun4i_drv_node_is_frontend(struct device_node *node)
